@* The cookie policy (S2.15). Keep the table in step with the API: PlayerAccountExtensions sets both cookies.
   If a cookie is added or changed, raise CookieBanner.PolicyVersion so everyone sees the banner again. *@
@page "/cookies"

<PageTitle>Cookie policy | ByteBait</PageTitle>

<main class="cookie-page">
    <h1>Cookie policy</h1>

    <p>
        ByteBait only uses cookies that are strictly necessary for the site to work. They don't need your consent,
        and they are set without you clicking anything. We don't use cookies for tracking, statistics or ads,
        and no cookies are shared with anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>

    <div class="cookie-table">
        <table>
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th scope="col">Name</th>
                    <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
                    <th scope="col">Lifetime</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>bytebait_login</code></td>
                    <td>Keeps you signed in, so your catches, money and aquarium are saved on your account. Set when you sign in or create an account.</td>
                    <td>7 days after you were last active. Deleted when you sign out.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><code>bytebait_antiforgery</code></td>
                    <td>Protects your account against forged requests from other websites (CSRF).</td>
                    <td>Until you close the browser.</td>
                </tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <p>
        Both cookies can only be read by ByteBait's server, only over HTTPS, and are never sent along when another site links to us.
    </p>

    <h2>Local storage</h2>

    <p>
        When you choose <strong>Got it</strong> on the cookie notice, your browser remembers it in local storage
        (<code>bytebait_cookie_notice</code>), so the notice isn't shown again. It stays until you clear your browser's site data
        and is never sent to the server.
    </p>

    <h2>If this changes</h2>

    <p>
        If ByteBait ever adds cookies that aren't strictly necessary, such as statistics, we will ask for your consent before they are set,
        and the cookie notice will be shown again.
    </p>

    <p>
        You can delete cookies in your browser's settings at any time. Without the login cookie you will just have to sign in again.
        ByteBait follows the Danish Agency for Digital Government's
        <a href="https://digst.dk/tilsyn/sporingsteknologiomraadet/cookievejledningen/" rel="noopener">guidance on cookies</a>.
    </p>

    <a href="/">Back to home</a>
</main>
